    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_3937",
      "reading_order": 5398,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 113.0,
        "t": 729.79,
        "r": 528.1300000000001,
        "b": 706.2
      },
      "content": "CAUTION: Never remove and then install a replacement DCC and formatter at the same time. Doing so will cause the printer to become unstable."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_3938",
      "reading_order": 5399,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 113.00002,
        "t": 696.79,
        "r": 533.7700100000002,
        "b": 673.2
      },
      "content": "If a replacement DCC and formatter must be installed, first remove and install the formatter. Test operate the printer, and then if necessary install a replacement DCC."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_3939",
      "reading_order": 5400,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 113.0,
        "t": 663.79,
        "r": 529.72,
        "b": 628.2
      },
      "content": "IMPORTANT: Take note of all empty connectors on the PCA before disconnecting any wire harnesses or flat-flexible cables (FFCs). Some empty connectors might not be visible until other items-like the harddisk drive-are removed, so pay close attention while removing the formatter and accessory items."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_3940",
      "reading_order": 5401,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 113.0,
        "t": 617.29,
        "r": 528.2900000000003,
        "b": 593.6999900000001
      },
      "content": "M501: Disconnect all of the connectors and FFCs, remove four screws (callout 1), and then remove the formatter."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_3941",
      "reading_order": 5402,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 113.0,
        "t": 343.42,
        "r": 529.4900000000004,
        "b": 319.83
      },
      "content": "M506/E50045/M507/E50145/M527/E52545/M528/E52645: Disconnect all of the connectors and FFCs, remove four screws (callout 1), and then remove the formatter."
    },
